    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion, mini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen coding in Go recently and writing a fmt.Println or calling a function, the list of options pops up and when I select it, it doesn't complete and I have to type (). When I do that, I get the following error.\n\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...vim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua\n:2345: Index out of bounds\nstack traceback:\n[C]: in function 'nvim_buf_get_text'\n...vim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2345: in function 'session_sync_cu\nrrent_tabstop'\n...vim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2139: in function 'session_init'\n...vim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1339: in function 'call_in_insert_\nmode'\n...vim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1337: in function 'insert'\n...m/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1400: in function <...m/site/pack/\ndeps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1350>\n\n### Reproduction\n\nWhile typing out terms in Golang like fmt.Println, the list of completion options comes up. Upon selecting, the error pops up. I then have to ESC out of it and then type my () to finish it. ",
