            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Hmm, it is not happening today. If it happens again I will attempt to screenrecord it.\n\nClosing until then.\n\n---\n\nOne possible condition I thought this might have been possible is at the buffer end. Following [session lifecycle](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-snippets.html#minisnippets.default_insert-sessionlifecycle) (especially the \"What is allowed but not officially supported/recommended:\" part section's bottom) it works as expected. I *can* see the error if doing something like this:\n- At the end of the buffer type and accept `fmt.Println()`. This starts a snippet session.\n- Inside parenthesis type and accept another `fmt.Println()`. This starts nested session.\n- Go into the Normal mode (while snippet session is still active) and delete the whole line (**which is known to not work**). It shows the error in the issue.\n\nIf this is the way you reproduced this, then following session lifecycle is the answer here. I.e. do not delete text of the snippet if there is an active session. You can stop the session manually by pressing `<C-c>` in Insert mode.",
